course: dictionary
lesson: 9469
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. The words around the word are your clues. «Italy became one state in 1861» means a country with its own government. Here state is not a mood or a mess, because a country cannot be upset or untidy.
explain: Now look at «She was in a state because she had lost her bag.» The clues are upset and lost, so in a state means very upset. Compare this with «The state of your bedroom!», which means very messy. Ask yourself: what does the sentence feel like? Upset and worried, or untidy and messy? Then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: Some words are commands in tests. «State the answer clearly» tells you to say or write the answer clearly, with no working needed. The word state is a command, not a place or a feeling. When you see state in a question, look for words like clearly, whether, or the number.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A state can be a condition, like «a state of mess» or «a calm state».
fact: A state can be one of the parts a country is divided into, each with its own government, such as in the USA or Australia.
fact: «In a state» means very upset or very messy (casual, UK and Ireland).
fact: To state something means to say or write it clearly and formally. In science, the states of matter are solid, liquid and gas.
exercise: «Italy became one state in 1861.» What does state mean here? | *A country with its own government | A tidy, calm room | A test question | A mood, like being upset
exercise: «She was in a state because she had lost her bag.» What does in a state mean? | *Very upset | Very quiet, almost silent | Very tidy | Very calm and happy
exercise: Your teacher says, «State the answer clearly.» What does state mean? | Draw a picture of it | Work it out in full, step by step | *Say or write it clearly
test: The Rus name first meant the ruling group, then «the whole state». In «the whole state», state means: | A sort of mood | A tidy room | *A country and its government | A type of school
test: Which of these is one of the states of matter? | Colour | Shadow | Noise | *Gas
exam: «State whether the statement is true.» What does state mean in this command? | *Say or write clearly | Read it silently | Draw a diagram | Guess a quick answer
